{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/4980","id":3820728174,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLW-eZs7ju69u","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4980","diff_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4980.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4980.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4980","number":4980,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[drawer] Drive swipe gestures natively to stop per-frame re-rasterization","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.com/atomiks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes #4863\r\n\r\n### Problem\r\n\r\nWhile a Drawer was open, every swipe `touchmove` re-rasterized the sheet's content instead of staying compositor-only. The `touchmove` bubbled into React's delegated touch system, and processing it there made Chrome invalidate and repaint the document and full-screen popup once per move (~2 paints per move). The translate was already a cheap composited transform — the repaints came from the event-dispatch path.\r\n\r\n### Fix\r\n\r\nDrive the swipe from a native, capture-phase `touchmove` listener. Once the Drawer claims the gesture it calls `stopPropagation()` so the move never reaches React's delegated handlers, forwarding it via a typed `moveFromNativeTouch` hook method. Propagation is preserved for cases the Drawer must not hijack (native scroll, range inputs, pinch-zoom, text selection). `getDragTransform` also moves to `translate3d`. No consumer CSS or workarounds required.\r\n\r\n### Results\r\n\r\n[Heavy drawer stress benchmark](https://mui-2026-drawer-performance.netlify.app/) (800-node payload, includes Vaul), headless Chromium, 20× CPU slowdown, paired same-session runs, medians:\r\n\r\n| Lib | Total busy | Paint | Paint ev | Avg move task |\r\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\r\n| Base UI (before) | 981 ms | 341 ms | 78 | 17.1 ms |\r\n| Base UI (after) | 631 ms | 70 ms | 6 | 8.9 ms |\r\n| Material UI | 723 ms | 328 ms | 79 | 14.4 ms |\r\n| Silk | 586 ms | 80 ms | 0 | 4.2 ms |\r\n| Vaul | 1121 ms | 86 ms | 6 | 10.2 ms |\r\n\r\nBase UI before → after: paint 341 → 70 ms (−79%), paint events 78 → 6, avg move task 17.1 → 8.9 ms (−48%), total busy −36%. The per-move content re-rasterization is gone; paint no longer scales with the heavy content.\r\n\r\nNotes: numbers reflect main-thread work during the gesture. `Total busy` = all main-thread time in the swipe window; `Avg move task` = per-move input-handler latency — not comparable across libraries (Silk travels via native scroll, so it offloads the drag to the compositor and delivers fewer JS moves). Material UI's `SwipeableDrawer` keeps an 800-node paper mounted while closed, which inflates absolute numbers for every row equally, so treat cross-library absolutes loosely; the Base UI before/after delta is unaffected.\r\n\r\n## Before\r\n\r\n<img width=\"638\" height=\"378\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-10 at 9 51 44 am\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c847e2c1-b2a9-483e-9500-d46885154f93\" />\r\n\r\n## After\r\n\r\n<img width=\"569\" height=\"379\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-10 at 9 52 25 am\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c421343-9c7f-4650-a4e4-33b337178bbb\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n\r\n- Handle swipe moves in a native capture-phase `touchmove` listener and call `stopPropagation()` so they don't reach React's delegated handler. Native scroll, range inputs, pinch-zoom, and text selection still propagate.\r\n- Add `moveFromNativeTouch` to `useSwipeDismiss` so the native listener feeds the gesture without a synthetic React event.\r\n- Switch the swipe transform to `translate3d`.","created_at":"2026-06-08T02:32:03Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T00:09:47Z","closed_at":"2026-06-10T00:09:41Z","merged_at":"2026-06-10T00:09:41Z","merge_commit_sha":"5b51e399674834dfd6dbf6d4988323fcd89a53bf","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"colmtuite","id":805073,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNTA3Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/805073?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite","html_url":"https://github.com/colmtuite","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"flaviendelangle","id":3309670,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzMDk2NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3309670?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/flaviendelangle","html_url":"https://github.com/flaviendelangle","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/flaviendelangle/followers","